{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall write them on the mezuzot of your house and in your gates.</b> So that you remember them at the time of entering and exiting. <b>On the mezuzot</b> — I might think two mezuzot; Rabbi Yitzhak says, behold it says, ״ונתנו על שתי המזוזת ועל המשקוף״ — this establishes a principle: every place where it says מזוזת it is only one, until Scripture explicitly specifies two mezuzot. <b>On the mezuzot</b> — our Rabbis said: opposite the shoulder-blades of a person, at the start of the upper third, and toward the outside." "<b>On the mezuzot of your house.</b> On the mezuzah of your entrance — on that side from which you enter first, namely the right, for a person leads with his right leg first." "<b>And in your gates.</b> Like <b>your house</b> — just as your house is a place of dignity, so every place of dignity, excluding a lavatory, a stable, a straw house, and the like."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:59.105081226Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}